{
  "dn28:0.1": "Long Discourses 28 ",
  "dn28:0.2": "Inspiring Confidence ",
  "dn28:1.0": "1. Sāriputta’s Lion’s Roar ",
  "dn28:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "dn28:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Nāḷandā in Pāvārika’s Mango Grove. ",
  "dn28:1.3": "Then Sāriputta went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "dn28:1.4": "“Sir, I have such confidence in the Buddha that I believe there’s no other ascetic or brahmin—whether past, future, or present—whose direct knowledge is superior to the Buddha when it comes to awakening.” ",
  "dn28:1.5": "“That’s a grand and bold statement, Sāriputta. You’ve roared a definitive, categorical lion’s roar, saying: ",
  "dn28:1.6": "‘I have such confidence in the Buddha that ",
  "dn28:1.7": "I believe there’s no other ascetic or brahmin—whether past, future, or present—whose direct knowledge is superior to the Buddha when it comes to awakening.’ ",
  "dn28:1.8": "What about all the perfected ones, the fully awakened Buddhas who lived in the past? Have you encompassed their minds to know that ",
  "dn28:1.9": "those Buddhas had such ethics, or such qualities, or such wisdom, or such meditation, or such freedom?” ",
  "dn28:1.10": "“No, sir.” ",
  "dn28:1.11": "“And what about all the perfected ones, the fully awakened Buddhas who will live in the future? Have you encompassed their minds to know that ",
  "dn28:1.12": "those Buddhas will have such ethics, or such qualities, or such wisdo